course: dictionary
lesson: 7946
title: One word, many jobs: rebel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do different jobs depending on the sentence. Rebel can be a noun (a person), a verb (an action), or an adjective (a describing word). Read the words around it, because they are its context and they tell you which job it is doing. «The rebels hid in the hills.» Rebels are people here, so it is a noun.
explain: «They decided to rebel against the king.» Here rebel is an action: they will fight or refuse to obey. Its verb forms are rebel, rebels, rebelled and rebelling, so «The soldiers rebelled last year» is the past tense.
explain: In «the rebel army», rebel describes the army. Try a simple meaning in the place of the word, such as «people who fight against those in power». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A rebel is a person who fights against the government or the people in power.
fact: A rebel can also be someone who does not follow rules or what others expect.
fact: To rebel means to refuse to obey the people in charge.
fact: «Rebel» can be a noun, a verb, or an adjective, as in «rebel army».
fact: Informally, «my tummy rebelled» means the body refused the food.
exercise: «The rebels took over the old fort.» Who are the rebels? | Children who play in the fort | Tourists who visit castles | Farmers who grow apples | *People who fight against those in power
exercise: «Ben decided to rebel against the rules at school.» What does rebel mean here? | *To refuse to follow the rules | To write a long story | To paint a picture of the school | To run very fast
exercise: «My tummy rebelled after the spicy curry.» What does rebelled mean here? | The tummy laughed loudly | The curry was cooked too long | The tummy went to sleep early | *The body refused the food
test: «The rebel group met in secret.» What job does rebel do in this sentence? | Person (noun) | Joining word (conjunction) | *Describing word (adjective) | Action word (verb)
test: A teenager argues with parents and ignores the house rules. What is the teenager doing? | Cooking dinner | Sleeping late | Painting the hallway | *Rebelling against them
exam: Read «The rebels marched into town.» What does rebels mean? | Tired walkers on a long trip | Old friends who visit | *People who fight against those in power | Bright lights in the sky
